        <!--RESEARCH-->
        <div id="gray-bg-section" style="height:3151px;">
        
        	<div id="section-icon" style="background:url(../images/research-icon.png) no-repeat 50% 0px;"></div>
            <div id="section-title">Research</div>
            <div id="section-text-middle" style="text-align:justify;">It was key to perform extensive research to gather valuable insights that can be leveraged to create an optimal design solution. Since we were designing a service for a theme park, we figured that it would be best to start by actually visiting one to perform an extensive analysis on it. We compiled a general list of what we wanted to understand for our project. The more information we could gather, the more it would benefit our design process.</div>
        	<div id="section-subtitle-large" style="margin:0 auto;padding:15px 0px 15px 0px;width:880px;border-top:2px solid black;border-bottom:1px solid black;">Park visit objectives</div>
        	<div id="section-text" style="height:400px;border-bottom:1px solid black;padding:30px 0px 30px 0px;font-size:14px;">
            	<div style="display:inline;width:250px;float:left;"><div id="red-text-header">1</div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">End-to-end experience</font>We wanted to understand a general experience flow of accessing, entering, experiencing, and exiting the park. This starts all the way from the customer purchasing the ticket, either online or at the entrance, up to the point when they finally exit the park to head home. Understanding this journey and all of its details helps reveal useful information and all of the touch points along the way that we can utilize to our advantage.</div>
                <div style="margin:0px 0px 0px 65px;display:inline;width:250px;float:left;"><div id="red-text-header">2</div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">Park layout</font>It was important to understand the entire layout of the park. This included not only the main attractions and zones but also the locations of restaurants, bathrooms, parking lots, entrances, exits, pathways, and any other defining areas within the park boundaries. Although provided maps generally define most of this, more areas that are generally not highlighted should be documented. It would also be great to note any designated meeting spots or locations that people generally tend to define as such.</div>
                <div style="margin:0px 0px 0px 65px;display:inline;width:250px;float:left;"><div id="red-text-header">3</div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">Park signage</font>What areas in the park have signed posted? What are the consistent signs displayed throughout the park? It's important to note all of these as they can potentially be used to notify visitors about any important information that we may want to disclose (i.e. - app download information and instructions).</div>
            </div>
            <div id="section-text" style="height:330px;clear:both;border-bottom:2px solid black;padding:30px 0px 30px 0px;font-size:14px;">
            	<div style="display:inline;width:250px;float:left;"><div id="red-text-header">4</div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">User interviews</font>These included everyone at the park: visitors, parents, children, staff. We want to conduct these with a wide demographic to understand behaviors, interests, and personal possessions that they carry at the park. An example of questions that I intiially put together can be seen by clicking on the following link:<br /><br /><a href="pdf/user-interviews.pdf" target="_blank" class="link">Sample of user interview questions</a></div>
                <div style="margin:0px 0px 0px 65px;display:inline;width:250px;float:left;"><div id="red-text-header">5</div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">Park visitor documents</font>What do visitors receive when they arrive and enter the park? Beyond the brochures, map, and ticket, is there anything else that should be brought to our attention? Gathering these documents that are intimate touch points with users can potentially be utilized to help us in some way.</div>
                <div style="margin:0px 0px 0px 65px;display:inline;width:250px;float:left;"><div id="red-text-header">6</div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">Park technology</font>Since the business owner wanted to be economical in this effort, we wanted to realize the available technology that currently exists in the park. From stationary devices like cameras, televisions, speakerphones, and sirens to those that are mobile such as cell phones, radio phones, and any other potential devices that can be utilized.</div>
            </div>
            
            <div id="section-subtitle" style="margin:auto;width:880px;border-bottom:2px solid black;padding:60px 0px 60px 0px;text-align:center;">We divided this list of objectives amongst our team so that everything will be completed efficiently and each of these elements would receive the necessary focus that is needed to harvest pertinent information.</div>
            
            <div style="clear:both;height:0px;"></div>
            
            <div style="margin:0 auto;height:150px;width:880px;border-bottom:1px solid black;padding:30px 0px 30px 0px;">
                <div id="section-subtitle-large" style="float:left;width:305px;padding:30px 0px 30px 0px;">Essential<br />tools</div>
                <div id="section-text" style="float:right;width:575px;padding:30px 0px 30px 0px;">In order to conduct our park visit effectively and efficiently, it was important to bring the proper equipment to assist us in completing our objectives successfully. Below are some of the necessary elements we would need to simplify this trip.</div>
            </div>
            
            <div style="clear:both;height:0px;"></div>
            
            <div id="section-text" style="padding:30px 0px 0px 0px;color:#5c5c5c;border:0px solid red;">
            	<div style="width:250px;float:left;">
            	<ul class="red-squares">
              		<li class="red-squares"><b>Digital cameras with both photo and video capability</b></li><br />
              		<li class="red-squares"><b>Notepads and pens for note-taking</b></li><br />
                    <li class="red-squares"><b>Strategically designed interview questionnaires unique to each subject (parents, children, visitors, staff, etc)</b></li><br />
              	</ul>
                </div>
                <div style="width:250px;float:left;margin:0px 0px 0px 65px;">
                <ul class="red-squares">
              		<li class="red-squares"><b>Voice recorders for user interviews</b></li><br />
                    <li class="red-squares"><b>Incentive for users to partake in user interviews. One proposal is conducting them at a restaurant, a common mid-day rest location, and provide a complimentary meal for their time.</b></li><br />
              	</ul>
                </div>
                <div style="width:250px;float:right;">
                <ul class="red-squares">
              		<li class="red-squares"><b>Consent forms for user interviews</b></li><br />
              		<li class="red-squares"><b>Computers to document information</b></li><br />
              	</ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div style="clear:both;height:60px;"></div>
            
            <div style="margin:0 auto;height:150px;width:880px;border-top:2px solid black;border-bottom:1px solid black;padding:30px 0px 30px 0px;">
                <div id="section-subtitle-large" style="float:left;width:305px;padding:30px 0px 30px 0px;">Market<br />exploration</div>
                <div id="section-text" style="float:right;width:575px;padding:30px 0px 30px 0px;">Beyond the park visit, we can also gather rich information from competitive or like-minded product services. It's ideal to conduct this step after the park when we have a better idea of park logistics - how people behave, what tools exist at the park, etc. This information fuels us with more targeted searches on market products and services that are applicable to our project.</div>
            </div>
            <div id="section-text" style="height:700px;border-bottom:1px solid black;padding:0px 0px 30px 0px;font-size:14px;text-align:left;">
                    <div style="display:inline;padding:60px 0px 0px 0px;width:175px;float:left;"><div class="circle-gray" style="background:url(images/market-research-icons.png) no-repeat 25px 30px;"></div><div style="height:30px;"></div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">Other theme park services</font>By analyzing the services available at other theme parks, we can understand what positive and negative practices they are carrying which can provide great fundamental guidlines when we design our project. One example is the <a style="font-size:14px;" href="http://miami.cbslocal.com/2013/01/08/disney-magic-spreads-with-electronic-magicband-bracelet/" target="_blank" class="link">My Disney Experience at Disney Theme Parks</a>.<br /><br />Although the electronic bracelet wouldn’t apply to our project because of our constraint that doesn’t allow children to wear devices, the accompanying app provides useful tools like the Fastpass booking capability which entices users to download it.</div>
                    <div style="margin:0px 0px 0px 60px;display:inline;padding:60px 0px 0px 0px;width:175px;float:left;"><div class="circle-gray" style="background:url(images/market-research-icons.png) no-repeat -193px 28px;"></div><div style="height:30px;"></div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">Mobile apps</font><br />With the plethora of apps available, they are a great resource to understand interactive elements that help users in similar or related scenarios. Apps related to maps, tracking, or hunting come to mind. Hunting apps may seem like an odd one but locating a lost child without tracking capabilities may inherently carry the same habits and processes.</div>
                    <div style="margin:0px 0px 0px 60px;display:inline;padding:60px 0px 0px 0px;width:175px;float:left;"><div class="circle-gray" style="background:url(images/market-research-icons.png) no-repeat -421px 28px;"></div><div style="height:30px;"></div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">Related products &amp; services</font>What other service processes can be investigated and leveraged to incorporate into our project? Services such as mall security or the work of detectives comes to mind. Perhaps we can take the time to interview someone that practices in one of these professions to provide us with some valuable insight.</div>
                    <div style="margin:0px 0px 0px 60px;display:inline;padding:60px 0px 0px 0px;width:175px;float:left;"><div class="circle-gray" style="background:url(images/market-research-icons.png) no-repeat -646px 26px;"></div><div style="height:30px;"></div><font style="display:block;font-weight:bold;color:black;">Technology</font><br />After realizing the technology that exists at the park, how can it all be leveraged to collaborate with the app we are going to build? Also, what new technologies that exist be applied to work in tandem with existing ones?</div>
            </div>
            
            <div id="section-subtitle" style="margin:auto;width:790px;padding:60px 0px 60px 0px;text-align:center;">Upon the valuable information gathered throughout the aforementioned studies, we can proceed to begin conceptualizing and visualizing it all which will help produce general principles and guidelines for what we want to build.</div>
            
        </div>
         <!--END RESEARCH-->
        
